      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To examine the immediate effects of patellar taping on pain and relative activity of vastus medialis obliquus to vastus lateralis in subjects with patellofemoral pain and patellofemoral joint malalignment."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "DESIGN",
          "content": "Pre- and post-treatment design, with order of testing determined randomly."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "SETTING",
          "content": "Outpatient physiotherapy department."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "SUBJECTS",
          "content": "Fifteen subjects with patellofemoral joint pain and malalignment."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "INTERVENTIONS",
          "content": "With and without patellar taping with a standard force of application."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "MAIN OUTCOME MEASURES",
          "content": "Pain and surface EMG activity ratio of vastus medialis obliquus to vastus lateralis during single-legged semi-squat with 20% of extra body weight loading."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "There was a significant decrease in anterior knee pain (p < 0.001) and vastus medialis obliquus to vastus lateralis activity ratio (p = 0.05) during single-legged standing after patellar taping."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "Patellar taping can reduce pain in people with patellofemoral pain syndrome and patellofemoral malalignment but it decreases the relative activity of vastus medialis obliquus to vastus lateralis. Such a decrease in relative activity of vastus medialis obliquus after taping implies that it may not be suitable to combine patellar taping with vastus medialis obliquus facilitative exercise training."
        }
      ]},
